WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.222
"The Efficacy, Safety, and Side Effects
of Botox and Facelifts"

00:00:07.222 --> 00:00:09.960
Anti-aging medicine
is one of the fastest growing

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.080
medical specialties,
and often targeted at women,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.660
who are urged to restore
their youthful appearance

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.880
by "any and all
available means."

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.980
This includes surgery.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.560
92 percent
of cosmetic procedures

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.340
are performed on women,
most commonly Botox, fillers,

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.760
and laser or chemical
peel skin resurfacing,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.480
but millions in the U.S. undergo
cosmetic surgery every year,

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.660
including hundreds of thousands
of face-lifts.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.620
There's no consensus on
the best face-lift technique.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.860
None have been shown to be
definitively better than others.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:47.040
A systematic review found that
most of the studies

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.740
on the newest techniques
were mere case series,

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:53.160
one of the lowest levels
on the hierarchy of evidence,

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.160
basically composed of a string
of glorified anecdotes.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.420
According to one of the largest
and most up-to-date analyses,

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.480
face-lifts are considered
relatively safe when performed

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.580
by a board-certified
plastic surgeon,

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.040
with surgical complications
only happening

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.280
in about 1 in 20 cases,
most often hematomas,

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.380
where blood collects
under the skin flaps,

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.120
or minor infections.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.860
Serious infections,

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.320
like facial necrotizing
fasciitis

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.840
caused by flesh-eating bacteria
are rare,

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.000
as is pyoderma gangrenosum,

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.360
a disfiguring, skin ulcerating
autoimmune disease

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.760
that can be triggered
by face-lift surgery.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:35.220
Other uncommon consequences
include scarring, hair loss,

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.160
and injuries
too gruesome to show.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.260
Nerve injuries occur in at most
a few percent of cases,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.780
but only about
1 in 1000 procedures

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.300
may result in permanent
facial nerve injury.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.640
About two-thirds of face-lifts

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.860
are performed under
general anesthesia,

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.440
which is associated with
a greater risk of complications.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.140
The most important way
to mediate risk

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.660
is to refrain from smoking.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:04.200
Smoking can increase the risk
of skin flap necrosis,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.900
or tissue death,
up to twenty-fold.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.220
Patients should refrain from
smoking at least a month before

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.320
and month after surgery.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.920
Tempering expectations
is also important.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.600
Approximately 1 in 3 women

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.900
experience a period
of postoperative depression,

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.300
but this may just be
in reaction to

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.700
the temporary distortion
and discoloration

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.620
of swelling and bruising
after surgery.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:33.000
The most profitable
cosmetic procedure is Botox,

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.380
in the billions,

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.060
as well as the most common,

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:39.600
performed more than four million
times a year in the US alone.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.740
It all started when
a group of surgeons noticed

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:47.280
that patients with Bell's palsy,
facial paralysis,

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.200
didn't have as many wrinkles.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.420
So what about
injecting minute amounts

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.120
of the nerve-blocking toxin
that causes botulism

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:57.420
to paralyze a few
facial muscles on purpose,

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:01.200
and a multibillion-dollar
industry was born.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:03.420
The effect is temporary,

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.700
typically lasting
three to four months

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.820
until the body can grow back
new nerve terminals.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:13.020
In response to cases of
respiratory failure and death

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.420
occurring hours or even weeks
after injection,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:19.140
in 2009 the FDA mandated
a black box warning

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.240
regarding the potential
spread of the toxin

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.320
resulting in death

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.180
from swallowing
and breathing difficulties

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:27.660
occurring hours, days,
or weeks after injection.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.840
However, most of these
complications were tied

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:34.860
not to cosmetic uses
but to treating muscle spasms--

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.540
for example in cerebral palsy.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:41.400
For wrinkles, only 30 to 60
units of the toxin may be used,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.720
compared to an average of about
180 for severe muscle spasms,

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.480
though still a far cry
from the estimated lethal dose

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.580
of perhaps 3,000 units.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:54.540
The dose is given in MU,
"mouse units,"

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:57.840
with one MU being the amount
capable of poisoning

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.600
half of a group
of albino mice to death.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:05.640
In studies, less than
1 in 2,000 Botox procedures

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.620
resulted in complications,

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.520
which can include droopy
eyelids, double vision,

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.060
an asymmetrical smile,
or the Spock,

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.360
a devilish curvature of
the outer portion of the brow.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.620
Unfortunately, not all such
procedures are performed

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.240
under such
controlled conditions.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.820
In many states,
there is surprisingly little

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.580
or no regulation
as to who can deliver Botox,

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.920
leading to a rapid increase
in injections

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.540
by nonmedical personnel.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:36.000
In one five-ish year period,

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.800
about 30,000 complications
allegedly tied to Botox

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.300
were reported to the FDA,

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:46.200
most commonly pain, swelling,
and eyelid or eyebrow drooping,

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:49.440
but most adverse effects are
transient and self-limited.

